{"records":[{"id":"fd823rnnmm","title":"Molecular Dynamics Dataset of Wild-Type and Mutant15.1 scFv–Fubc Complexes","description":"This dataset contains molecular dynamics (MD) simulation data and associated computational files for the wild-type (WT) and Mutant15.1 single-chain variable fragment (scFv) in complex with the Fubc epitope of the dengue virus envelope protein.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-11-03T18:15:26.952Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fd823rnnmm","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fd823rnnmm"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Md Fahim","last_name":"Khalid","orcid":"0009-0001-4052-3207"},{"first_name":"Satyajit","last_name":"Podder","orcid":"0009-0000-0038-3740"},{"first_name":"Barnali","last_name":"Halder","orcid":"0009-0004-0005-7215"},{"first_name":"Rinkoo Devi","last_name":"Gupta","orcid":"0000-0003-1156-9596"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Structural Biology","Molecular Dynamics","Computational Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y2x7c6x76n","title":"Emerging therapy for dengue","description":"Dengue fever is acute febrile diseases, it’s caused by one of four closely related virus serotypes of the genusare Flavi virus, family Flaviviridae. Each serotype is sufficiently different that there is no cross-protection and epidemics caused by multiple serotypes can occurs. It’s transmitted to humans by the mosquito.\nThe incidence of dengue has grown around the world in recent a period of ten years. However, several classes of agents are in under investigation as potential anti-dengue drugs, including direct host modulators, antivirals, and RNAi therapeutics. These anti-dengue drugs in development will be reviewed here.\nKeywords: Dengue viruses, Aedes mosquito, Treatment\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-05-31T06:11:11.028Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y2x7c6x76n","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y2x7c6x76n"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jitesh N patil","last_name":"Narendra patil","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dengue Virus"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vhzzzc6m36","title":"Diagnostic Discrimination of Zika and Dengue-2 Infection by High-Throughput TCR Sequencing","description":"The Zika virus has been listed as a global health threat by the World Health Organization due to its association with congenital birth defects. Current FDA-approved diagnostics are unable to distinguish between infection with Zika and other flaviviruses. Here, we report on the computational identification of virus-associated TCRβ-sequencing using high-throughput sequencing prior to and after infection with Zika or Dengue-2 viruses.  Computationally identified T cell receptor sequences were shown to be virus-specific and used to develop a diagnostic assay that correctly diagnoses Zika and Dengue-2 infected in mice with 97% accuracy. These results identify populations of TCR sequences specific for Zika and Dengue infection that can be used for diagnostic purposes, and serve as an important proof-of-principle, providing a novel platform for accurately diagnosing Zika virus infection. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-09-25T17:03:23.996Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vhzzzc6m36","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vhzzzc6m36"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kyle","last_name":"Wolf","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"cv9c4gzdy9","title":"S5. Transmission potenital (Index P) data","description":"Transmission potential (index P)  quantifies the risk of dengue virus transmission in a specific region, taking into account climate-based factors such as temperature and humidity, which directly influence the breeding, survival, and biting behaviour of the mosquito vectors responsible for spreading the virus. This index provides insight into how favourable environmental conditions are for dengue circulation in a given area.  The spatio-temporal estimates of transmission potential for African countries and territories used in this review were developed by Nakase et. al (2023) .","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-10-17T09:43:47.366Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/cv9c4gzdy9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/cv9c4gzdy9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Gaspary","last_name":"Mwanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/05bk57929","name":"Stellenbosch University","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Systematic Review"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y6xjbjcgz8","title":"Docking of Dengue virus type 1 or West Nile Virus surface antigen with SARS-CoV-2 Spike antibody","description":"Docking of SARS-CoV-2 Spike antibody with surface antigen of Dengue virus type 1 or West Nile Virus using ClusPro and ZDOCK","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-09T09:56:09.616Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y6xjbjcgz8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y6xjbjcgz8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Subhajit","last_name":"Biswas","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virology","West Nile Virus","Dengue Virus","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"g23k3t8c83","title":"Thoudam et al, 2022, Noncanonical PDK4 action alters mitochondrial dynamics to affect the cellular respiratory status","description":"Datasets related to the study \"Noncanonical PDK4 action alters mitochondrial dynamics to affect the cellular respiratory status\" by Thoudam, Chanda et al. 2022, in the journal PNAS","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-10T16:20:58.491Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/g23k3t8c83","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/g23k3t8c83"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"themis","last_name":"thoudam","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Dipanjan","last_name":"Chanda","orcid":"0000-0003-0685-187X"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Basic Science","Mitochondrial Function"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65g5z7fpdc","title":"Clinical data from a unique case of SARS-CoV-2 and Dengue virus coinfection with heterozygous Beta Thalassemia","description":"We report a 30-year-old man with hemoglobinopathies coinfected with SARS-CoV2 and Dengue virus from Bangladesh. Dengue virus was detected by ELISA. Covid-19 was confirmed by RT-PCR and Hemoglobin Electrophoresis revealed heterozygous beta-thalassemia. The patient was treated successfully at Dhaka Hospital in icddr,b during Covid-19 emergency response with symptomatic supportive treatment for Covid-19 and appropriate fluid therapy for dengue fever in response to daily hematocrit level. After 21 day, the patient’s RT-PCR for Covid-19 became negative. For thalassemia, the patient was advised to have genetic counseling and family screening on discharge. The data complies here were gathered from the patient management record file.\n\nThe possibility of coinfection should be considered during the Dengue fever epidemic along with the confirmatory tests for Covid-19, when any alarming signs supporting possibility of dengue fever are found in an individual. Fluid therapy for dengue fever must be maintained with utmost care to avoid adverse effect from Covid-19-Dengue coinfection and careful monitoring of oxygen saturation during the sick period of this type of case should be performed with importance.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-06-08T15:09:57.176Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65g5z7fpdc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65g5z7fpdc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Md Rezaul","last_name":"Hossain","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Monira","last_name":"Sarmin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lubaba","last_name":"Shahrin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zannatun","last_name":"Nyma","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tahmeed","last_name":"Ahmed","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mohammod Jobayer","last_name":"Chisti","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Case Report","Medical Care in Bangladesh","Clinical Management","Bangladesh","Dengue Virus","Thalassemia","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hk76kcmyp9","title":"LINF_300034900","description":"NADH-ubiquinone oxidoreductase complex I subunit | NDUFS6 ortholog; Leishmania infantum (strain JPCM5)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-07-19T19:21:35.688Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hk76kcmyp9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hk76kcmyp9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","grant_id":"PID2020-117916RB-I00"}],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y4bj5f6ky4","title":"LINF_350042100","description":"NADH-ubiquinone oxidoreductase complex I subunit | NDUFB7 ortholog; Leishmania infantum (strain JPCM5)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-08-22T11:43:35.853Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y4bj5f6ky4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y4bj5f6ky4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","grant_id":"PID2020-117916RB-I00"}],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"khft7ks78h","title":"LINF_180005800","description":"NADH-ubiquinone oxidoreductase complex I subunit | NDUFA9 ortholog; Leishmania infantum (strain JPCM5)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-05-10T12:05:24.353Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/khft7ks78h","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/khft7ks78h"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","grant_id":"PID2020-117916RB-I00"}],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":129796,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":100,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":129796,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":129262,"restricted":64,"embargoed":470},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2151},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1476},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":597},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":451},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":437},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":412},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":406},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":360},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":287},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":255}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":127192},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","nam